From d98dbe9a4f75ca9a41b8dda8f2fd6c304fbf907f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:01:47 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 289/410] Unified: fixes from the first-time-user test of 0.6.9
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Assembly: the part of the file goes into its assembly and is held
  (grounded); parts put in are free. Snapping a held part moves the other
  one instead, and "Swap" never moves (or turns over) a held part.
- More of a part in an assembly: Ctrl+C / Ctrl+V, "Another of This Part",
  "Copies in a Grid" (rows × columns, the four corners in one go). A
  double-click on a part in the tree picks it instead of opening its file.
- Hole: further clicks on the face add holes; the panel lists them with
  their distances from the left and bottom edge to type.
- After "also the edges in the same direction" the bar stays; a digit goes
  into its number field wherever the focus is, never turning the view.
  Python's addSelection with a point is a pick at that point.
- Drawing: only real holes get the hole callout (not R corners), one line
  per size; hole positions from the left/bottom edge, also as a command;
  the title block in Japanese; PDF export starts with the file's name.
- DXF: the drawing's frame and title boxes are no outline; lines that do
  not close are reported and nothing is made.
- Screws, washers and nuts follow their hole; the drawing's center lines
  follow the holes. Closing the last 3D view closes the file (asking to
  save); a file opens on its 3D view.
- Views move without animation when a panel opens (the first click on a
  plane hits); the model is kept in view after a typed length.
- A thinner screw than the hole goes through with a nut (M5 in ⌀6: M5×25).
- Missing icons are logged, not notified; catalog icon paths of the build
  machine map to this installation; "Processing..." translated; search
  rows with the same name say where they work.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
